4. Router4 and router5 have **no route at all** to 172.18.x.x (grep returns empty)
5. Only r0, r1, r2, r3 have compensating kernel static routes (proto=none) for 172.18.50/24 and 172.18.51/24, forming a one-way chain to router6
6. Router6's ripd process is stable (no crashes, 6+ min uptime), but with nothing to advertise (split-horizon suppresses all routes received from router3 back to router3), it sends no meaningful periodic updates, causing the r3-r6 adjacency to appear as a bouncing/absent source on router3

